{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"84ef3f1d789bc123","name":"card_event_stretch_the_line","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/events/card_event_stretch_the_line","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"STRETCH THE LINE","text":"Add a LEGIONS to your support line then Intel equal to friendly LEGIONS.","flavorText":"The Battle of Mokra, which took place on September 1st, 1939, was a significant engagement during the German invasion of Poland and marked one of the first major clashes between Polish and German forces during WWII. Situated near the town of Mokra in southern Poland, the battle unfolded as part of the broader defensive efforts against the German advance. Polish defenders, consisting of the Volhynian Cavalry Brigade and elements of the 7th Infantry Division, confronted two German panzer divisions and two infantry divisions. Despite being outnumbered and outgunned, the Polish forces skillfully employed anti-tank weapons, including 37mm anti-tank guns and improvised Molotov cocktails, to inflict significant casualties on the German armored units. By the end of the battle, the Poles had destroyed over 50 German tanks and inflicted 800 casualties in one of the only Polish victories of the war. The determined resistance at Mokra disrupted the German timetable and temporarily halted their advance, allowing Polish forces to regroup and reinforce their defenses in other sectors. While ultimately unable to prevent the German conquest of Poland, the Battle of Mokra demonstrated Polish resolve and ingenuity in the face of overwhelming odds.","faction":"Poland","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_stretch_the_line","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_stretch_the_line_title","SourceString":"STRETCH THE LINE","LocalizedString":"STRETCH THE LINE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_stretch_the_line_text","SourceString":"Add a LEGIONS to your support line then Intel equal to friendly LEGIONS.","LocalizedString":"Add a LEGIONS to your support line then Intel equal to friendly LEGIONS."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_stretch_the_line_history","SourceString":"The Battle of Mokra, which took place on September 1st, 1939, was a significant engagement during the German invasion of Poland and marked one of the first major clashes between Polish and German forces during WWII. Situated near the town of Mokra in southern Poland, the battle unfolded as part of the broader defensive efforts against the German advance. Polish defenders, consisting of the Volhynian Cavalry Brigade and elements of the 7th Infantry Division, confronted two German panzer divisions and two infantry divisions. Despite being outnumbered and outgunned, the Polish forces skillfully employed anti-tank weapons, including 37mm anti-tank guns and improvised Molotov cocktails, to inflict significant casualties on the German armored units. By the end of the battle, the Poles had destroyed over 50 German tanks and inflicted 800 casualties in one of the only Polish victories of the war. The determined resistance at Mokra disrupted the German timetable and temporarily halted their advance, allowing Polish forces to regroup and reinforce their defenses in other sectors. While ultimately unable to prevent the German conquest of Poland, the Battle of Mokra demonstrated Polish resolve and ingenuity in the face of overwhelming odds.","LocalizedString":"The Battle of Mokra, which took place on September 1st, 1939, was a significant engagement during the German invasion of Poland and marked one of the first major clashes between Polish and German forces during WWII. Situated near the town of Mokra in southern Poland, the battle unfolded as part of the broader defensive efforts against the German advance. Polish defenders, consisting of the Volhynian Cavalry Brigade and elements of the 7th Infantry Division, confronted two German panzer divisions and two infantry divisions. Despite being outnumbered and outgunned, the Polish forces skillfully employed anti-tank weapons, including 37mm anti-tank guns and improvised Molotov cocktails, to inflict significant casualties on the German armored units. By the end of the battle, the Poles had destroyed over 50 German tanks and inflicted 800 casualties in one of the only Polish victories of the war. The determined resistance at Mokra disrupted the German timetable and temporarily halted their advance, allowing Polish forces to regroup and reinforce their defenses in other sectors. While ultimately unable to prevent the German conquest of Poland, the Battle of Mokra demonstrated Polish resolve and ingenuity in the face of overwhelming odds."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","spawnCardName":"card_unit_legion_pol","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Poland/Summer_24/t_stretch_the_lines.t_stretch_the_lines","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Polish WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/STRETCH_THE_LINE.STRETCH_THE_LINE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":349.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_stretch_the_line_photo","SourceString":"Polish artillery near Mokra, 1939. ","LocalizedString":"Polish artillery near Mokra, 1939. "},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"Image needed to be customized","isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"count","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_stretch_the_line